messages[8]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hello, um, hi Anjali? This is Reyansh. I wanted to double‑check what happens when my policy hits 30 Sept 2027.
  user_2,[00:10] Hi Reyansh, yes I’m here. So the current policy is set to expire on that date, and unless you request a renewal, it will just lapse.
  user_1,[00:20] Okay… so if it lapses, do I need to do anything special? Like cancel it formally?
  user_2,[00:30] No formal cancellation needed – the system will mark it as expired automatically. [sighs] Just make sure any pending claims are submitted before 90 days after the service date.
  user_1,[00:45] Got it. And the premium – do I have to pay anything after the expiry?
  user_2,[00:55] Once the expiry date passes, the monthly premium stops. If you decide to re‑enroll later, we’ll set up a new premium based on the rates at that time.
  user_1,[01:10] One more thing – the tele‑consultation coverage, does that continue after expiration, or does it end same day?
  user_2,[01:20] It ends the day the policy expires. After that you’d need a new plan for tele‑consults. Anything else I can help with?